From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:02:57 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 06/48] net: airoha: ploam: the PLOAM trailer is a CRC-8, not a
 BIP-8

The header described the 13th octet of a PLOAM message as a BIP-8
checksum. G.984.3 defines it as a CRC-8 over the first twelve octets
with the generator x^8 + x^2 + x + 1; BIP-8 is the per-frame parity
carried in the PCBd and reported through REI, which is a different
mechanism. Fix the comment so nobody looks for the PLOAM check in the
BIP counters.

Comment only, no functional change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ploam.h | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ploam.h b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ploam.h
index 5f580a3..da618f3 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ploam.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ploam.h
@@ -16,7 +16,8 @@
  * Layout: value[0][31:24]=ONU-ID, [23:16]=MsgType, [15:0]=content[0-1]
  *         value[1]                               = content[2-5]
  *         value[2]                               = content[6-9]
- * The BIP-8 checksum (byte 12) is computed/verified by hardware.
+ * The 13th octet is the G.984.3 PLOAM CRC-8 (generator x^8 + x^2 + x + 1),
+ * not a BIP-8. The hardware computes it upstream and checks it downstream.
  */
 #define PLOAM_WORDS		3
 #define PLOAM_CONTENT_LEN	10
